<title>SPAIN: Spain private pension funds rise 36 pct to end-Sep.</title>
<headline>Spain private pension funds rise 36 pct to end-Sep.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish private pension fund assets were 2.53 trillion pesetas at the end of September, a rise of 36.0 percent compared to the year-ago month, the Association of Institutions of Collective Investment (INVERCO) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The number of participants rose 14.0 percent to 1.92 million.</p>
<p>The annual weighted average yield of the private pension funds was 10.19 percent and 8.96 percent over the past five and three years, respectively.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
